Z||000000||Richard Parnell||10-12-1999||05:07 PM||||My 87 SC was hit on the right rear and right front (sandwiched) in an accident before I bought the car and the fascias split from the impact.   I am getting ready to order a new front fascia but I want to be sure that I get the identical facsia I now have. I like the way it rolls under to a ground spoiler rather than the normal straight down look.  I was looking at what the Fiero store offers in the way of replacements but they don't look like they have the coupe style.  I want to be sure they have the correct one before ordering and perhaps having to ship it back.  (I live in Hawaii, so the shipping is not cheap nor always fast) If Fiero store does not have the correct one, does anyone in our knowledgable crowd know where to order the correct fascia.  For the rear I will need to order a fascia that will accomodate dual exhaust as I am proceeding with my plans for a V8 conversion,  maybe the GT?  I'm not absolutely sure also that the frame was not bent in that accident.  What type of measurements can I do on the car without removing the entire body to check? Thanks for all of you being out there to answer questions like this. ||||reg||11
